<p>Russian authorities say the Russia-flagged LNG tanker Arctic Metagaz exploded, caught fire and sank in the Mediterranean Sea between Libya and Malta while carrying about 61,000 tonnes of liquefied natural gas. Moscow alleges Ukrainian naval drones struck the vessel, and Russia’s transport ministry says the drones launched from the Libyan coast. Russia’s transport ministry said all crew members were safely evacuated. The sinking adds to growing concerns about the security of energy shipping routes and infrastructure as the war continues. Some outlets described the ship as sanctioned by the US and EU as part of what they call Russia’s “shadow fleet” used to move oil and gas despite restrictions.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Igiq3qCip0ozp_T9Nm6IxVEDPs9lxLOMNgzdxjeEMc4XTazX6gAN_rlN3XQRN9aC5obpTNPvojiVCnoWdR-QK0IoPZVS2GYd42dKedDoVKoXQPxyBng1FSS9FwzVHOQPtxaxLE0t-iwtQm-uEH32plXw-vraUDHyKgveXb8jJV-4gEBTeh5_qCzNoHkH-xoW7FlBdw' alt='File image used to illustrate Russia-Ukraine war coverage in The Hindu’s report.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Location and timing details differ by outlet: The Guardian put the explosions on Tuesday night about 150 miles (240km) off Libya, RT said the incident happened close to Malta’s territorial waters, and the BBC reported the ship sank between Libya and Malta.</li><li>Route detail: RT reported that Russia’s transport ministry said the Arctic Metagaz was sailing from Murmansk when it was hit.</li><li>Extent of loss: The Hindu cited a statement saying the tanker “completely sank” between Libya and Malta.</li><li>Separate drone activity in Russia: The Guardian reported that Saratov region governor Roman Busgarin said Ukrainian drones damaged civilian sites, prompting temporary closures at Saratov airport and other airports in southern and central Russia; the report also mentioned three injuries.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Russia’s transport ministry (as cited by RT): The ministry said Ukrainian unmanned boats launched from the Libyan coast struck the Arctic Metagaz while it was sailing from Murmansk, and that the crew was evacuated safely. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/russia/633810-russian-lng-tanker-attack-ukraine/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Vladimir Putin (Russia): Putin described the alleged strike as a “terrorist act” and said Ukraine was preparing sabotage against the Blue Stream and TurkStream gas pipelines, according to RT and The Guardian. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/04/putin-accuses-ukraine-of-attacking-gas-tanker-that-exploded-and-sank-off-libya'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Ukraine (government): Ukraine had not commented on the tanker sinking at the time of The Guardian’s reporting. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/05/ukraine-war-briefing-putin-blames-ukraine-for-sinking-of-tanker-off-coast-of-libya'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Libyan officials (as cited by BBC): Libyan officials said the ship went down between Libya and Malta after explosions and a fire, without attributing responsibility in the BBC report. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cr5ll27z52do'>BBC</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/russia-blames-ukrainian-sea-drones-for-attacking-tanker-that-sank-in-mediterranean/article70704650.ece'>Russia blames Ukrainian sea drones for attacking tanker that sank in Mediterranean</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/05/ukraine-war-briefing-putin-blames-ukraine-for-sinking-of-tanker-off-coast-of-libya'>Ukraine war briefing: Russia claims LNG tanker in Mediterranean hit by drones</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/russia-blames-ukrainian-drones-for-attack-on-lng-ship-in-mediterranean'>Russian LNG tanker sinks in Mediterranean, Moscow blames Ukrainian drones</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/russia/633810-russian-lng-tanker-attack-ukraine/'>Ukrainian attack on Russian LNG tanker a ‘terrorist act’ – Putin</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cr5ll27z52do'>Russia blames Ukrainian naval drones as tanker sinks in Mediterranean</a> - bbc.com</li></ul>